    "result_text": "Done. The build passes green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `checkDigit` field to the owner response \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the decimal digits of the `customerCode`.\n\nChanges:\n1. **`util/CustomerCode.java`** (new) \u2014 `checkDigit(String code)` computes the standard Luhn check digit over the decimal digits in the code, ignoring the `-` separators. This mirrors the algorithm the test uses.\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression that populates `checkDigit` from `CustomerCode.checkDigit(owner.getCustomerCode())`, alongside the other derived response fields.\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared the `checkDigit` property (readOnly `int32`, 0\u20139) on the Owner schema so the generated `OwnerDto` has the field.\n\nThe new field flows out through the existing `POST /api/owners` \u2192 `GET /api/owners/{id}` path with no pipeline changes needed, since it's a purely derived response value. `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` and the full suite are green.",
